<h3>CamToggle</h3>
<form class="form-horizontal" onsubmit="return false;">
    <div class="control-group">
        <label class="control-label">systemd service(s)</label>
        <div class="controls">
            <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" placeholder="auto" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.camtoggle.services">
            <span class="help-block">
                <strong>Leave empty for auto-detection</strong> (hover the camera icon to see the detected
                service). Otherwise, one or more comma-separated services. OctoPi ≥ 1.0: <code>camera-streamer-libcamera</code>
                (Pi Cam) or <code>camera-streamer-usb-default</code>. OctoPi &lt; 1.0: <code>webcamd</code>.
                Crowsnest: <code>crowsnest</code>.
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="control-group">
        <label class="control-label">systemctl path</label>
        <div class="controls">
            <input type="text" class="input-large" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.camtoggle.systemctl">
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="control-group">
        <div class="controls">
            <label class="checkbox">
                <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.camtoggle.persist">
                Keep state across reboots (re-applied when OctoPrint starts)
            </label>
            <label class="checkbox">
                <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.camtoggle.auto_on_print_start">
                Turn the camera on when a print starts
            </label>
            <label class="checkbox">
                <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.camtoggle.auto_off_print_done">
                Turn the camera off when a print ends
            </label>
        </div>
    </div>
    <h4>How it works</h4>
    <p class="muted">
        The camera icon in the navbar stops or starts the camera's systemd service. When the service is stopped,
        the camera, CPU, memory and network bandwidth it used are freed. Green icon = running, grey = stopped.
        The webcam stream reloads after each change, and the state is synced across all open browsers.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
        Without "Keep state across reboots", the camera follows the system at boot (usually on).
        Timelapses fail while the camera is off: use "Turn the camera on when a print starts" if you record them.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
        Documentation, troubleshooting and source code:
        <a href="https://github.com/blaisebarrette/Pi-cam-toggle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/blaisebarrette/Pi-cam-toggle</a>
    </p>
</form>
